DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions calculate the error function of _x.

     The eerrff(), eerrffff(), and eerrffll() functions calculate the error function of
     x; where

           erf(x) = 2/sqrt(pi)∗integral from 0 to x of exp(-t∗t) dt.

     The eerrffcc(), eerrffccff(), and eerrffccll() functions calculate the complementary
     error function of _x; that is eerrffcc() subtracts the result of the error
     function eerrff(_x) from 1.0.

